these  little guys are efficient especially  maggots and blowflies which can consume  60% of the body's tissue in just a few  weeks hopefully you died someplace nice  like a hospital so your disembodied  ghost doesn't have to watch all these  horrible things happen to your body  speaking of ghosts what happens to the  part of you that's not physical is there  even such a thing many cultures and  religions believe in the idea of a soul  or a spirit or some form of incorporeal  manifestation of your conscious self  separate from the physical body to keep  things simple we'll use the word soul to  represent all these terms there are lots  of fascinating ideas about what happened  to this sole it would take way too long  to cover them all so we'll just look at  three common perspectives Christians  largely believe that depending on how  you lived your life your soul will be  sent either to eternal paradise with God  in heaven or to eternal torment in hell  this belief varies by denomination with  some people believing that you just need  to be baptized to go to heaven some  claiming that you have to do good works  while you're alive and still others  believing that hell doesn't exist at all  statistically about 31% of all humans on  earth identify as Christian and  therefore likely believe some variant of  the heaven or hell idea the next largest  group by number of adherents is Islam  which accounts for 23 percent of the  global population Islam shares many  similarities with Christianity or vice  versa  depending on how you want to look at it  they're both Abrahamic religions and  share similar perspectives on much of  their faith they do differ somewhat in  terms of beliefs about the afterlife  many Muslims believe that after you die  your soul remains with your body in your  grave where you'll receive visions of  your fate until one day Allah raises all  the dead from their graves to judge all  the souls and send them either to  paradise or to hell  whereas many Christians believe their  souls are transported instantly to their  eternal fate Muslims got the short end  of the stick and have to stew for a bit  in their dead bodies on the bright side  that means more time before you have to  go to hell if you were naughty of course  this is only one of several Islamic  interpretations of the process of death  another perspective on death comes from  the Buddhists Buddhism asserts that life  is cyclical when you die your spirit is  reincarnated into a new body which could  be anything from another human to an  insect this process then repeats over  and over and over again until the soul  achieves enlightenment when a soul  reaches enlightenment they will leave  behind their mortal coil and reach  nirvana which is seen as an  incomprehensible indescribable and  inconceivable place the idea of  reincarnation is very appealing to a lot  of people including many Westerners who  were raised Christian it's not hard to  see why the idea of death is scary and  despite all of our many explanations of  what may happen after death we can't be  certain the Buddhist idea that we could  come back and live many more lives is  very comforting ok we've looked at a few  religious explanations for what happens  after death but what about for those of  us who don't identify as religious well  if we're looking strictly at natural  explanations for biological functions  it's most likely that nothing happens  after death your consciousness is tied  to your brain and when your brain ceases  to function you cease to exist  have been Studies on the phenomenon of  so-called near-death experiences but  obviously the results of these studies  are inherently flawed since the  responses have to come from someone  whose brain was literally shutting down  that being said the results are  interesting and worth noting in some  instances people who have been brought  back from the brink of death reported  walking towards a bright light which  many religious people take to mean  ascending towards heaven other people  report nothing at all they were awake  then it was like they fell into a  dreamless sleep and woke up again some  things many reports of near-death  experiences have in common is the  sensation of floating upwards out of  your body or seeing old friends or  relatives or watching scenes from your  life flash before your eyes while  medical experts have many hypotheses for  why exactly some people have these  near-death experiences there's not  really a sure answer yet scientists are  fairly certain these experiences are  just the spasms of a dying brain  flooding your nervous system with  chemicals in a losing battle against  death but they still need a lot more  data to figure out the finer details of  what occurs in the moments before we die  for a lot of people who don't believe in  the afterlife and even for many who do  death can be really scary one good quote  from Mark Twain might help a little he  said I do not fear death I had been dead  for billions and billions of years  before I was born and had not suffered  the slightest inconvenience from it so  whatever you believe live your life in a  way that makes you happy makes others  remember you fondly and in general just  be the best version of you you can be  one way to improve yourself is by  learning new skills which is why I  always recommend checking out Skillshare  Skillshare is an online learning  community for creators with over 20,000  classes and everything from photography  to graphic design to productivity  marketing fine art and more I love  Skillshare because any time I'm bored I  can just put on a class and learn  something worthwhile a premium  membership gives you unlimited access to  high-quality classes on useful topics so  you can improve your skills unlock new  opportunities and do the work you love  I'm actually working on my own intro to  photography course I'm not going to give  you an estimate of when it'll be done  because it's taking much longer than I  expected but it'll be available for you  to watch at some point in the near  future join the millions of students  already learning on Skillshare today  with a special offer just for you guys  get two months of Skillshare completely  free to start learning amazing new  skills today visit skill share by  following the link below  [Music]
 

